# The opening of the game: the title over the dark sea, then (on a new
# voyage) the night the lantern pulled you from it. Played by the Opening
# node in scenes/prototype/sea.tscn. Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.
#
# A cutscene is a conversation whose @ cues stage the scene. Lines wait for
# the Interact button; cues that take time (a fade, a wait, a clip) hold the
# script until they're done. Every cue is listed in
# scripts/cutscene/cue_list.gd.
#
# Where things are, so you can change them without touching this file:
# - Shots (where the camera goes) and marks (where people stand) are
#   Marker3D nodes. The bunk room's are in scenes/prototype/ship.tscn under
#   Shots and Marks; the rescue's are in scenes/prototype/intro/rescue_set.tscn.
# - Clips (@play, @start) are animations. The underwater ones are in
#   scenes/prototype/intro/underwater.tscn: open it, select Clips, and the
#   timeline at the bottom of the editor shows them. Each moves the set's
#   camera too, so a clip is also a shot.
# - Sounds (@sound) are the players under SoundCues in sea.tscn. Some have
#   no recording yet (plunge, bell, flare, deep_note, gasp):
#   they're silent until one is put where the player's Recording points.
# - The title is her nameboard at the stern: the letters, the hook, the
#   lantern on it and his clips (takes_watch, hears, welcome, to_the_rail and
#   the ones at the rail), the rail's shots and marks, and camera_goes_over are in
#   scenes/prototype/intro/stern_watch.tscn.
# - His looks (@look) are listed in scripts/companion/lantern_face.gd.
#
# To tune one beat: set Start Section on the Opening node to its name and
# the game opens there. While it runs, F8 reads this file again and replays
# the section you're in.

# Her name. The lantern on his hook at the stern, swinging, lights the
# carved board a few letters at a time. It waits for any button. With a
# saved voyage it asks whether to carry it on or start a new one; a new one
# asks who you are, then he hears something.
~ start
@hide heron
@play takes_watch
@look hook_lantern tired
@shot the_board cut
@fade in 3.0
@wait_for any Press any button
@sound confirm
? saved_voyage
-> voyage_menu
-> who_are_you

# With a saved voyage: carry it on, or start again. A new voyage leaves the
# old save until you next sleep in your bunk, which replaces it.
~ voyage_menu
- Continue your voyage -> carry_on
- Start a new voyage -> who_are_you

# A saved voyage: he turns from her name to the lit windows, pleased to see
# you. Then to black, and the Opening loads the voyage and shows which day it is.
~ carry_on
@continue_voyage
@look hook_lantern pleased
@play welcome
@wait 0.8
@show heron
@fade out 0.8
@play off_watch
@shot free cut

# A new voyage: who are you, a boy or a girl? Asked over her name, and it
# waits for the answer.
~ who_are_you
@who_are_you
-> the_stern

# The Prologue's first scene (docs/prologue.md, #182). A quiet night
# first. Then he's seen something: faint lights, far down in the water. The
# swinging stops and the camera draws back from her name to the stern, the
# black sea and the rain, and the captain at the wheel above. He calls up to
# him. (The shots are markers in scenes/prototype/intro/stern_watch.tscn:
# TheBoard, TheStern and TheWheel. The captain stands on its Wheel mark.)
~ the_stern
@play takes_watch
@shot the_board cut
@look hook_lantern tired
@place heron wheel
@show heron
@wait 1.6
@look hook_lantern surprised
@play hears
@grave on
@shot the_stern
@wait 1.2
@look hook_lantern pleased
lantern: There you are...
@play looks_out
lantern: I knew I hadn't imagined it.
lantern: Captain? I think I've found something.
@shot the_wheel cut
heron: Something, or another one of your little lights?
-> to_the_rail

# He lifts off the hook, settles beside the captain and invites him over
# before leading him to the rail. The two flights have separate clips in
# stern_watch.tscn so he can hold at the wheel while the player reads.
~ to_the_rail
@shot the_stern cut
@look hook_lantern determined
@play to_captain
@face heron at_wheel
@shot the_wheel cut
lantern: Captain. Come take a look.
@shot the_quarter cut
@start to_the_rail
@send heron beside_him
@wait 2.4
@shot side_by_side cut
@walk heron beside_him
@look hook_lantern calm
@start looks_over_the_rail
lantern: Look.
-> the_grave

# The camera goes past him, out over the water and down, and the sea gives
# way to what's under it: the Grave of the Lanterns. Thousands of them,
# empty, some broken, some caught in great chains, a few still glowing like
# dying stars, and no bottom. (The set is
# scenes/prototype/intro/grave.tscn; its camera moves are the clips
# over_the_grave, that_one, passes_below and finds_the_hand. The move over
# the side is the clip camera_goes_over, which carries the shot OverTheSide.)
~ the_grave
@shot over_the_side cut
@start camera_goes_over
@wait 1.5
@stage grave cut
@play over_the_grave
lantern: There must be hundreds of them.
heron: Thousands, most likely.
lantern: I wonder how long they've been down there.
heron: Longer than either of us.
@play that_one
lantern: Wait. That one...
-> something_down_there

# Cut back to the rail. He leans further, and something rings, far
# below. (at_the_rail and the captain's place put them back at the rail, so
# this beat can be started on its own while tuning.)
~ something_down_there
@stage off cut
@play at_the_rail
@place heron beside_him
@shot his_lookout cut
@look hook_lantern worried
lantern: Captain, I think there's something down there.
@shot captain_at_rail cut
heron: What do you hear?
@shot his_lookout cut
@look hook_lantern worried
@play leans_over_the_rail
@sound ring
@wait 1.8
@look hook_lantern surprised
lantern: That's strange.
-> the_shape

# Something moves beneath the ship: far down, something too big to be
# anything passes under them, seen only by what it hides, and the lanterns
# rock in its wake.
~ the_shape
@start steadies_at_the_rail
@shot over_the_side cut
@start camera_goes_over
@wait 1.5
@stage grave cut
@say_in 2.5 heron 2.6 Back away from the rail.
@say_in 5.6 lantern 2.2 I think I saw—
@play passes_below
-> the_hand

# Something drifting amongst the dead lights. At first it looks like
# another broken lantern. Then: a hand.
~ the_hand
@stage grave cut
@play finds_the_hand
lantern: ...
lantern: Captain?
heron: What is it?
lantern: There's somebody in the water.
-> overboard

# Cut back to the rail. He shouts it, and the captain turns, too
# late: before he's finished, the lantern is over the rail and gone.
~ overboard
@stage off cut
@play at_the_rail
@place heron beside_him
@shot captain_at_rail cut
heron: What?
@shot his_lookout cut
@look hook_lantern determined
lantern: Somebody overboard!
@shot captain_at_rail cut
@face heron rail_perch
@say heron 1.4 Don't you dare—
@wait 0.7
@shot his_lookout cut
@start dives_from_the_rail
@wait 0.3
-> plunge

# The plunge. From out on the water: the storm sea, the ship's quarter, and
# one small point of light arcing out from her rail through the rain. It hits
# the water, and it's gone.
~ plunge
@look flying_lantern determined
@show flying_lantern
@shot the_plunge cut
@play off_watch
@start flies
@wait 1.45
@sound plunge
@wait 1.5
@hide flying_lantern
-> dark

# The dark. The storm stops dead as the water closes over, and he's
# already in it. Far above, a bell: somebody heard him.
~ dark
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@sound bell
-> light

# The light. A small warm thing comes through the surface, a long way off,
# and drives down through the dark to you, still warm and bright: the dive
# costs him nothing yet. His light finds dim shapes hanging all round:
# lanterns, like him. (The Prologue's Scene 1, #183.)
~ light
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern determined
@look sinking_lantern clear
@look sinking_lantern mended
@play lantern_appears
@play lantern_drives
@look sinking_lantern calm
@play lantern_arrives
-> finds_you

# He dips to look for a response. You don't answer.
~ finds_you
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern surprised
lantern: Hello?
@look sinking_lantern worried
lantern: Can you hear me?
@play searches_your_face
lantern: Oh, you're in a bad way...
-> tries

# He gets under you and heaves, and you go on sinking. He looks up at the
# surface, so far above, and back at you.
~ tries
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@say_in 1.2 lantern 2.4 Come on. Come on!
@play heaves
@look sinking_lantern worried
@play looks_up
@look sinking_lantern determined
lantern: Hold on. I've got you.
-> reach

# The reach. A flame can't reach through glass, so he opens his own door
# and his flame comes out into the shape of a hand, and holds it out to
# you. It waits for as long as it takes. You can take it at any moment.
~ reach
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play opens_door
@look sinking_lantern determined
@start reaches_out
@queue offered
@say_in 1.6 lantern 2.6 Here. Take my hand.
@wait_for interact Take his hand
@sound grasp
@look sinking_lantern calm
@play taken
-> it_catches

# The touch. A strange note through the water. He freezes, and his flame
# flares brighter.
~ it_catches
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern surprised
@play catches
lantern: Oh...
-> it_flows

# Then the light runs out of his hand into yours, along your arm, and you
# begin to glow. And a thinner thread of it sinks away from him, down to the
# dead lanterns far below (the Drain node): they're drawing on him too. He
# tries to pull away, and it holds, and his flame shrinks (#203).
~ it_flows
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern worried
@play flows
lantern: The lanterns down there...
lantern: they're calling my light.
@look sinking_lantern effort
@play pulls_back
@look sinking_lantern pleading
lantern: I can't...
lantern: I can't hold on to it.
-> the_deep_stirs

# All round, the dead lanterns flicker. A deep rumble. He looks down:
# something enormous shifts in the dark below, passing beneath the chains,
# shown only in the lightning.
~ the_deep_stirs
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern surprised
@start stirs
@wait 1.4
@hush on
@sound deep_note
@wait 1.6
@lightning
@wait 2.2
@lightning
@wait 2.8
@hush off
-> lets_go

# He looks back at you, almost out. He chooses, and lets the last of it go:
# a burst of gold that fills everything. White. Silence.
~ lets_go
@stage underwater cut
@muffle on
@look sinking_lantern tired
@play looks_back
lantern: I don't know who you are...
lantern: But I can't let you go.
@look sinking_lantern determined
@start lets_go
@wait 1.2
@hush on
@fade white 1.2
@stage off
@muffle off
@wait 2.5
-> asleep

# The white goes to black, and stays black for a while: how you came aboard
# isn't shown. Then, slowly, the bunk room at night, the storm outside: you
# asleep in your bunk, and the captain standing by its head, watching over
# you. The lantern is beside you, on the little table at the foot of your
# bunk (#206), small and blue, his light nearly all gone (#158).
~ asleep
@place heron bedside
@show heron
@face heron sleeping_you
@hide player
@show sleeping_you
@home lantern
@face lantern sleeping_you
@look lantern worried
set lantern_low
@shot in_your_bunk cut
@fade out 3.0
@wait 1.5
@hush off
@fade in 3.0
@wait 0.8
-> waking

# You wake on your own, with the captain standing over you by the head of
# your bunk (the Prologue's Scene 2, #184).
~ waking
@start wakes
@wait 1.6
-> you_look_up

# Still lying down, you look up: the captain, standing over you by the head
# of your bunk, the lantern on his table at its foot. The captain is the
# first to speak (#206).
~ you_look_up
@shot you_lying_down cut
@wait 0.6
heron: Ah. You're awake.
heron: Easy. Take your time.
@play stirs_in_bunk
@shot lantern_at_bunk cut
@face heron lantern
heron: You gave me a fright.
lantern: Did I?
heron: Both of you did.
-> by_your_bunk

# By the time we look round you're up, and he's there by your bunk; the
# lantern on the table at its foot, barely lit, but talking. He tries to
# float over to you and can't. The captain asks what you remember, and
# you've nothing to tell him. (Your answers are the replies you pick.)
~ by_your_bunk
@hide sleeping_you
@show seated_you
@face heron seated_you
@shot beside_your_bunk cut
@play stands_from_bunk
@place player bunk_stand
@hide seated_you
@show player
@wait 0.3
@face lantern player
@face heron player
@face player heron
@shot by_the_lantern cut
@wait 0.6
@look lantern pleased
lantern: I told you they'd wake up!
@face heron lantern
heron: You also told me you were perfectly capable of swimming.
lantern: I am!
@look lantern tired
heron: Clearly.
@look lantern surprised
lantern: Oh! Hello!
@go lantern lantern_tries
@wait 1.0
@look lantern tired
@go lantern lantern_sinks
@wait 0.9
@home lantern
@wait 0.8
lantern: Oh. That's not ideal.
heron: You've used nearly all your light.
lantern: I know.
heron: You could have left them.
@wait 1.0
lantern: I know.
@face heron player
@shot facing_him
heron: Do you remember anything?
- (Shake your head) -> your_name

~ your_name
heron: Your name?
- (Say nothing) -> where_from

~ where_from
heron: Where you came from?
- (Say nothing) -> how_you_ended

~ how_you_ended
heron: How you ended up in the water?
- (Look down) -> i_see

~ i_see
heron: I see.
@face heron lantern
@shot beside_your_bunk
heron: Well, whatever happened out there, you're fortunate he's as stubborn as he is.
@look lantern pleased
lantern: You're welcome.
heron: I wasn't thanking you.
@face heron player
heron: I need to take the wheel. When you're steady, come and find me.
heron: Let's see if we can get him warm again. Start with that book by your bunk.
-> yours

# Then the ship is yours. The captain goes up on deck to the helm, where you
# find him for the pot (the FirstQuest node in sea.tscn walks him there, and
# to the water butt for a drink now and then). The lantern has a word first,
# and points you to your book: it's on his table, by him (picking it up is
# data/dialogue/recipe_book.dlg, #206).
~ yours
@shot by_the_lantern
@look lantern tired
lantern: Don't mind him.
lantern: He's always like that.
lantern: Oh! And you left your book here. It's on the table, by me.
@shot free cut
